+### Height Query
+Height Query retrieves the height of the terrain at a given world coordinate $(x, z)$ by finding the containing chunk and querying its local height table [S3, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently mapping continuous world coordinates to discrete chunk-local height data [S3, unofficial].
+
+**Steps**
+1. Calculate chunk world position: `XChunkPos = floor(x / Chunk::m_XSize)`, `ZChunkPos = floor(z / Chunk::m_ZSize)` [S3, unofficial].
+2. Create `ChunkPosition` key and check if the chunk exists in `m_Chunks` [S3, unofficial]. If not, return -1 [S3, unofficial].
+3. Calculate local coordinates within the chunk: `localX = (x % Chunk::m_XSize + Chunk::m_XSize) % Chunk::m_XSize`, `localZ = (z % Chunk::m_ZSize + Chunk::m_ZSize) % Chunk::m_ZSize` [S3, unofficial]. This handles negative modulo correctly [S3, unofficial].
+4. Retrieve the chunk and call `chunk->GetHeight(localX, localZ)` [S3, unofficial].
+
+**Pitfalls**
+- **Negative Coordinates**: The modulo operation for local coordinates adds the chunk size before taking the modulo again to ensure positive indices for negative world coordinates [S3, unofficial].
+
